function guide(){if(state&&room){notify('Online clock keeps running. Drag to look, WASD to move; choose a response to lock it.');return;}const old=screen;view(panel(`<span class="eyebrow">FIELD GUIDE / READ THE FINE PRINT</span><h2>Make the call. Own the effect.</h2><p><strong>Move:</strong> WASD or arrow keys. Use Mouse look to capture the cursor (Escape releases it), or drag the scene to look. Q / R turn by keyboard. Shift moves faster and F toggles your flashlight. E inspects a nearby active terminal. Navigate to case offers an accessible shortcut. Click or tap a nearby terminal, patrol drone, holographic city map or coffee machine. E also interacts with the object at the centre of your view. Scan room outlines your active workstation for eight seconds. The direction indicator shows which way to turn and how far to walk. Drones acknowledge a tap by hovering and reversing their route.</p>${scoringGuide()}<p><strong>Investigation:</strong> Each case opens with a ten-second transmission. Inspect printed evidence documents or the evidence board to collect three source documents. Evidence helps your judgement without awarding points. Every timed question allows 50 seconds, at every difficulty; untimed solo play is available in setup. Evidence and this guide do not pause an active clock. Music changes with pressure and outcomes; Sound mutes it.</p><p><strong>Chikku’s optional lead:</strong> Greet her near the lift after the arrival clues. She can point out a loose queue slip at your active case desk. Use Field Tools → Chikku’s Find for directions, then compare the slip with the scheduler archive. No points are awarded and your legal decisions remain unchanged. Colleagues react to your recent decisions. Walking commentary mixes occasional jokes with source-reading hints; Playful Banter in Accessibility disables jokes while retaining useful hints.</p><p><strong>Case Operations:</strong> At the active table, compare witness accounts with their source records, inspect the three exhibits, preserve a read-only snapshot, trace BL-0116 and request a scoped hold. Earlier unsafe calls add a retry reconciliation task in later cases. These tasks are untimed. Use Case Journal for inspected clues and your next step. At dawn, make a separate final deduction from the recovered approval trail.</p><p><strong>Levels:</strong> Desk Rookie → Consent Detective (350) → Incident Commander (700) → Privacy Sentinel (1050) → Nightshift Legend (1400).</p><p><strong>Floors:</strong> Lift / Floors takes you to departments 47–50. Your objective names the destination. The yellow arrow appears on the active floor. Completing a case saves a checkpoint.</p><p><strong>History:</strong> only completed stories are remembered locally, per browser. Group selection prioritises stories unfamiliar to the most players. Clearing browser data clears that history. Usernames remain in memory and are not persisted.</p>${legalNote()}<div class="row">${button('back','RETURN',true)}${state?'':button('learn','FIELD INDUCTION · TUTORIAL')}</div>`),'guide');bind('#learn',tutorial);bind('#back',()=>{if(state){lastRender='';render();}else home();});}

